<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernardini Tomb</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bernardini Tomb is a princely burial of the early 7th century BCE at Praeneste, modern Palestrina, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latium">Latium</a>, found in 1876. With the nearby Barberini Tomb, it held gold, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> objects made in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, showing the wealth of the Orientalising period in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. Its contents are in the National Etruscan Museum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p></div>
